WEBVTT

00:01.070 --> 00:08.140
<i>Having sensed peace throughout the world,
Fushi awakens from a long slumber.</i>

00:08.730 --> 00:11.960
<i>He begins a new journey.</i>

00:11.960 --> 00:13.850
<i>He meets new people.</i>

00:14.360 --> 00:16.710
You can stay forever, if you want.

00:17.520 --> 00:20.660
I-If you insist...

00:24.700 --> 00:26.170
I want to die.

00:26.170 --> 00:29.560
<i>Her name was Mizuha.</i>

00:41.900 --> 00:43.440
Doesn't that hurt?

00:44.460 --> 00:47.220
You probably shouldn't ignore it.

02:27.000 --> 02:31.000
A Knot in the Soul

02:35.710 --> 02:38.250
Wh... What?

02:41.690 --> 02:42.840
Hey...

02:46.570 --> 02:47.930
Hey.

02:47.930 --> 02:49.980
That was so funny.

02:49.980 --> 02:52.100
You know in that video...

02:52.870 --> 02:55.240
What?! What do you think you're doing?

02:55.240 --> 02:58.300
Oh, sorry. It's just that you 
look like someone I know.

02:59.070 --> 03:01.560
Well? Has life been fun for you?

03:01.860 --> 03:04.410
What? Is that a question?

03:04.410 --> 03:05.710
Look, there she is.

03:05.710 --> 03:06.790
She's at it again?

03:06.790 --> 03:07.840
Right? She's crazy.

03:08.370 --> 03:09.240
Bye.

03:09.240 --> 03:10.240
Wait!

03:10.590 --> 03:12.760
Peaceful to the point of being boring.

03:12.760 --> 03:13.700
Mom.

03:14.020 --> 03:17.430
Someone ought to tell me if
there's something fun going on.

03:17.980 --> 03:21.440
Why aren't you waiting in
the nurse's office, Mizuha?

03:21.440 --> 03:23.300
Now, let's go to the hospital.

03:23.980 --> 03:25.630
So you're enjoying life.

03:26.100 --> 03:28.320
That's great.

03:37.070 --> 03:38.930
Dinner time!

03:43.540 --> 03:46.400
Who were you talking to earlier?

03:46.400 --> 03:49.250
The descendant of someone
I used to know, I think.

03:49.250 --> 03:50.710
I don't know her name.

03:50.710 --> 03:52.370
But I'm glad she seems to be doing well.

03:52.370 --> 03:53.680
Descendant?

03:53.680 --> 03:55.090
How old are you, Fushi-san?

03:55.090 --> 03:56.830
He's estimated to be 800.

03:58.500 --> 04:01.430
I borrowed a bunch of
books that mention Fushi.

04:01.710 --> 04:04.900
You're the legendary immortal
that awoke from a tree.

04:04.900 --> 04:07.330
A messenger of God! Right?

04:07.330 --> 04:10.080
Kazumitsu, what's this dish called?

04:10.080 --> 04:12.800
Hm? It's curry rice.

04:13.940 --> 04:17.910
So anyway, he randomly came up
to me and started talking to me.

04:17.910 --> 04:19.910
He was dressed weirdly, too.

04:19.910 --> 04:21.560
He must be from overseas, right?

04:21.560 --> 04:24.730
Have you developed a crush on this boy?

04:24.730 --> 04:27.020
No, it's nothing like that.

04:27.350 --> 04:29.240
We're moving, Mizuha.

04:29.240 --> 04:32.580
We'll be out by next month. Be ready.

04:42.070 --> 04:44.110
Hey, Fushi-san!

04:45.970 --> 04:47.940
Have you seen this video?

04:47.940 --> 04:51.790
This is called a video, huh? 
Everyone has one of these.

04:51.790 --> 04:53.620
No, this is a smartphone.

04:53.620 --> 04:54.520
Here.

04:55.740 --> 04:57.230
<i>Is this my tomb?!</i>

04:57.510 --> 04:58.760
Oh, Bon.

04:58.760 --> 05:00.050
Do you know him?

05:00.050 --> 05:01.110
He's with me.

05:01.110 --> 05:02.190
I knew it!

05:02.500 --> 05:04.470
<i>Hands up, thief!</i>

05:04.470 --> 05:05.760
<i>How dare you?!</i>

05:06.250 --> 05:07.470
<i>You!</i>

05:07.920 --> 05:09.690
<i>A Bonchien cosplayer!</i>

05:09.690 --> 05:10.990
<i>Take a picture with me!</i>

05:10.990 --> 05:12.340
<i>Can I have your autograph?</i>

05:12.340 --> 05:14.390
<i>What is wrong with you people?</i>

05:14.390 --> 05:17.050
<i>Fushi! Where are you?!</i>

05:16.220 --> 05:18.870
Isn't this the Uralis castle?

05:18.870 --> 05:21.590
There's a ton of these videos lately.

05:21.590 --> 05:24.880
It's a series of videos of people who
time-traveled from the Middle Ages.

05:24.880 --> 05:27.170
<i>Let me go! This is a mistake!</i>

05:27.170 --> 05:29.600
<i>I'm a soldier who served Uralis!</i>

05:30.030 --> 05:31.030
Kai!

05:32.160 --> 05:33.560
Hairo!

05:36.830 --> 05:39.760
<i>He's stealing booze!</i>

05:40.250 --> 05:42.450
<i>What the hell are you looking at?!</i>

05:42.770 --> 05:44.810
Messar!

05:44.810 --> 05:47.210
I just wanted to show him his hometown.

05:47.210 --> 05:50.310
I thought he'd handle it all right 
since he's a grown-up...

05:50.310 --> 05:51.960
Let's help them!

05:51.960 --> 05:53.820
Why don't we teleport them here?

05:53.820 --> 05:56.330
I can't. I'd need them to die first.

05:56.330 --> 05:58.330
Yikes. What's up with that rule?

05:58.750 --> 06:00.540
Oh, look at the comments.

06:01.050 --> 06:08.090
"If you know anything about this video,
please contact the Tasty Peach Foundation."

06:08.350 --> 06:10.050
That has something to do with Bon.

06:10.050 --> 06:12.500
We can email them, then!

06:11.280 --> 06:12.500
Hold it!

06:12.500 --> 06:14.560
Are you bringing even more people here?!

06:15.040 --> 06:17.120
How many more now?

06:17.120 --> 06:18.910
Um, eight...

06:18.910 --> 06:20.970
Wait, seven people and two animals?

06:20.970 --> 06:22.230
That's too many!

06:22.870 --> 06:29.440
Long ago, where I lived, there were things
that came to kill us just because we existed.

06:29.920 --> 06:35.650
My dream was to take the people I care about
to a place where those things didn't exist.

06:36.070 --> 06:40.250
This town—this home—is perfect.

06:40.250 --> 06:42.500
So I want to bring them here.

06:43.900 --> 06:46.910
Please, Kazumitsu?

06:47.670 --> 06:49.410
Why are you a small dog now?

06:49.410 --> 06:51.790
I'll leave if you say no.

06:51.790 --> 06:52.940
Don't go!

06:52.940 --> 06:54.890
Come on, Gramps!

06:54.890 --> 06:57.630
Look at him! He's so fluffy!

06:58.640 --> 07:00.680
But we don't have that much space.

07:00.680 --> 07:03.600
Oh, I can make more rooms.

07:05.850 --> 07:08.850
Maybe I ought to trust my
grandkids' instincts on this one.

07:09.190 --> 07:10.850
Thank you, Gramps!

07:10.850 --> 07:12.270
I love you!

07:25.080 --> 07:27.490
Is everyone really coming?

07:27.490 --> 07:29.970
Yup. That's what the Foundation told me.

07:29.970 --> 07:31.670
Listen, Fushi.

07:31.670 --> 07:34.170
There are a lot of people here.
You'd better not transform.

07:34.170 --> 07:34.960
Got it.

07:34.960 --> 07:38.720
What if it's a trap set by a secret organization 
pretending to be the Foundation?

07:38.720 --> 07:40.010
If it is...

07:40.010 --> 07:42.790
Fushi-sama and Aoki-sama?

07:42.790 --> 07:45.240
We're from the Tasty Peach Foundation.

07:45.240 --> 07:47.570
I'm Aoki Aiko. I'm the one who contacted you.

07:47.570 --> 07:49.730
Thank you for waiting.

07:49.730 --> 07:51.690
They're all waiting this way.

07:52.010 --> 07:55.180
What is this Tasty Peach Foundation business?

07:55.180 --> 07:58.900
We carry on the will of the
Uralis Kingdom and offer support.

07:58.900 --> 08:04.110
Our organization exists to pass down the
promise made by Prince Bon and Fushi-sama.

08:04.110 --> 08:10.010
We have been preparing for the day
when Prince Bon would return to life.

08:13.550 --> 08:16.430
Guys! It's been so long! How've you all been?

08:18.580 --> 08:20.640
How've we all been? You ass!

08:20.640 --> 08:24.300
You abandoned us in the middle of 
nowhere and did a shit job reviving us!

08:24.670 --> 08:28.270
You say that, but it looked to me
like you were enjoying yourself.

08:28.500 --> 08:34.480
I was living in prison until the
Foundation came to get me out.

08:34.480 --> 08:37.620
Why don't you say something?

08:37.620 --> 08:40.070
Hey, now, cut it out, Messar.

08:40.870 --> 08:43.480
Bon. You look fabulous.

08:43.480 --> 08:45.300
It's almost like you're someone else.

08:45.300 --> 08:47.830
I'm not used to it yet, though.

08:47.830 --> 08:49.350
Oh, don't say that, sir.

08:49.350 --> 08:51.740
You look great, Prince Bon.

08:51.740 --> 08:55.680
I find the customs and clothing
of this time distasteful,

08:55.680 --> 08:58.260
but it's necessary in order to blend in.

08:58.260 --> 08:59.520
Yup, yup.

08:59.520 --> 09:01.760
I know, right? I think so, too.

09:01.760 --> 09:03.970
Fen and Nixon? Are they there?

09:04.370 --> 09:05.930
Should I bring them back to life?

09:05.930 --> 09:07.140
That won't be necessary.

09:07.500 --> 09:11.570
They've made their own decision to stay in
their current state. They've accepted it.

09:11.570 --> 09:13.750
All right, then.

09:13.750 --> 09:16.430
Ooh, you're considerate, aren't you?

09:16.430 --> 09:17.540
What is it, Fushi?

09:18.280 --> 09:20.000
Oh, never mind.

09:20.430 --> 09:21.510
It's nothing.

09:22.070 --> 09:27.740
In any case, the best way to stay out of
trouble is to blend in and not get noticed.

09:27.740 --> 09:29.730
Get noticed?

09:29.730 --> 09:32.250
Easy for you to say. You don't
have to be in your own skin.

09:32.250 --> 09:35.170
I'm sorry, that was thoughtless of me.

09:35.170 --> 09:37.210
I'm not angry.

09:37.210 --> 09:38.980
I like the way I look.

09:40.930 --> 09:42.990
Thanks, Fushi.

09:42.990 --> 09:46.180
You didn't forget us.

09:46.180 --> 09:47.360
Gugu.

09:47.360 --> 09:48.690
Where's March?

09:48.690 --> 09:50.850
I thought she was with you in Yanome.

09:51.330 --> 09:52.810
March...

09:55.810 --> 09:58.400
We don't need to bring March here.

09:58.910 --> 10:01.870
She seems to have found a kind family.

10:02.180 --> 10:05.200
She's better off with them.

10:05.200 --> 10:07.330
Fu-chan!

10:07.330 --> 10:09.700
I'm here!

10:09.950 --> 10:11.910
March! But why?

10:11.910 --> 10:12.930
Why?

10:12.930 --> 10:15.560
These men showed up, so I came with them.

10:15.560 --> 10:17.130
Is something wrong with that?

10:17.130 --> 10:18.340
Well...

10:19.500 --> 10:20.510
Thank goodness.

10:20.940 --> 10:23.170
Thank goodness for nothing!

10:23.930 --> 10:27.640
Why the hell am I back in a kid's body?!

10:28.220 --> 10:30.480
Oh, good. It was a success.

10:30.480 --> 10:32.110
You call this a success?!

10:32.110 --> 10:34.930
I mean, you said before
that you wanted youth.

10:34.930 --> 10:38.530
I-I did say that, but I can't
believe you'd actually do it.

10:38.530 --> 10:43.530
Also, I made myself resilient to
poison for your sake, you know!

10:43.530 --> 10:45.000
Yeah, I know.

10:45.000 --> 10:48.750
How am I supposed to help
you in this flimsy body?!

10:49.120 --> 10:51.740
The world's peaceful now, Tonari.

10:52.260 --> 10:53.950
It was meant to show my appreciation.

10:54.230 --> 10:55.400
Should I not have?

10:57.410 --> 10:59.450
Nope. Imma sock you once.

10:59.450 --> 11:01.690
Yeah, get him! I'll give you a hand.

11:01.690 --> 11:02.890
Messar!

11:03.470 --> 11:05.050
How dare you lay a hand on Bon-sama?!

11:07.320 --> 11:08.510
Messar!

11:08.510 --> 11:09.690
Stop it!

11:09.690 --> 11:10.850
No violence!

11:10.850 --> 11:13.180
I'll calm them down!

11:14.150 --> 11:15.400
Fire!

11:15.400 --> 11:17.260
What do you think you're doing?!

11:17.260 --> 11:19.270
You're all under arrest!

11:30.960 --> 11:34.210
Shit, it's so cramped in here.

11:41.620 --> 11:43.130
Hey, isn't that...

11:46.780 --> 11:48.350
Senpai!

11:48.350 --> 11:50.530
Hey there.

12:02.810 --> 12:04.570
Well, come in.

12:04.860 --> 12:07.760
Remember when I said I fished up a weirdo?

12:07.760 --> 12:11.030
His friends are living with us now, too!

12:11.320 --> 12:14.580
Fushi, messenger of God,
and his warriors of light!

12:14.870 --> 12:17.010
I used to just live with two other people,

12:17.010 --> 12:19.650
but now there'll be nine more 
people and two animals.

12:19.650 --> 12:22.260
It's gonna be even more awesome!

12:26.340 --> 12:28.230
You two, get in the car!

12:28.230 --> 12:29.300
We're out of here!

12:29.300 --> 12:30.620
Don't worry.

12:30.620 --> 12:32.100
That bear's with me, too.

12:32.100 --> 12:34.250
I thought I'd have him help build new rooms.

12:34.250 --> 12:36.440
Oh, all right, then.

12:36.440 --> 12:38.310
No, that's not all right!

12:38.310 --> 12:41.390
What about our stuff?
Everything inside our house?!

12:41.390 --> 12:42.610
No problem.

12:42.610 --> 12:44.700
I'll just rebuild all of it.

12:54.150 --> 12:59.420
You sure have found some useful abilities
in the short time I haven't seen you, Fushi.

13:02.610 --> 13:03.910
Big!

13:04.200 --> 13:07.100
I kept the furniture the same and
made the place twice the size.

13:07.100 --> 13:08.770
You're amazing, Fushi!

13:08.770 --> 13:10.610
Thank you, Fushi-san!

13:11.020 --> 13:12.960
I never agreed to this.

13:12.960 --> 13:14.600
My apologies.

13:14.600 --> 13:18.050
I, Bon, will handle any complaints.

13:18.310 --> 13:20.270
What about <i>him</i>?

13:20.270 --> 13:22.300
You don't expect me to keep him here, do you?

13:22.300 --> 13:23.550
There's no way!

13:23.550 --> 13:25.480
Take him to the zoo or something.

13:25.480 --> 13:28.940
No! I'm not letting you take him anywhere!

13:29.990 --> 13:33.610
May I ask who owns the
forest behind the house?

13:34.330 --> 13:35.910
It's mine. Why?

13:35.910 --> 13:41.120
The Tasty Peach Foundation will front the
costs and deal with maintenance and upkeep.

13:41.370 --> 13:43.280
Please, mister.

13:43.280 --> 13:45.580
Let him stay, please, Gramps?

13:48.100 --> 13:50.050
You'd better look after him.

13:50.320 --> 13:51.440
Okay!

13:51.440 --> 13:53.270
Thank you, Gramps!

13:56.520 --> 13:58.920
That's all the lumber scraps.

14:01.820 --> 14:03.690
That's Gugu.

14:03.690 --> 14:06.630
He's super strong, 
and he can even breathe fire.

14:06.630 --> 14:07.880
He's crazy.

14:08.190 --> 14:11.370
Well, the Foundation will take it from here.

14:11.370 --> 14:13.020
That man's Bon.

14:13.020 --> 14:15.330
He's really important in Uralis, apparently.

14:15.550 --> 14:18.920
Hang on. May I have the scrap metal?

14:18.920 --> 14:21.310
That guy's a former weapon
craftsman named Kai.

14:21.310 --> 14:23.260
He has a really cool scar on his face.

14:23.260 --> 14:24.640
Yo, old man.

14:24.640 --> 14:27.100
Where's the closest brothel around here?

14:27.100 --> 14:29.240
Dunno. Find it yourself.

14:30.220 --> 14:32.600
I dunno what Messar does.

14:32.600 --> 14:34.320
I dunno if I like him much.

14:34.320 --> 14:36.860
Did you say something, kid?

14:38.010 --> 14:42.270
Hairo's fascinated by Grandpa's
dentures for some reason.

14:48.340 --> 14:52.210
March, I'll leave the ointment here.

14:52.210 --> 14:55.210
Thanks, Auntie—Big Sister Tonari.

14:55.480 --> 14:57.990
That smart-looking girl is Tonari.

14:57.990 --> 14:59.690
That's her pet, Ligard.

15:00.370 --> 15:02.930
The smallest of them is March here.

15:02.930 --> 15:05.720
The biggest is this white bear.

15:09.600 --> 15:13.550
So, what are you all up to in this world?

15:13.930 --> 15:15.850
Ah, y'know.

15:15.850 --> 15:17.940
We'll figure it out tomorrow.

15:17.940 --> 15:20.810
Aren't you going to fight evil
organizations or anything?

15:20.810 --> 15:22.890
Or help people in need?

15:22.890 --> 15:25.550
Sure, if we have the opportunity.

15:27.210 --> 15:31.360
Also, why've you been talking
to yourself all this time?

15:31.360 --> 15:33.160
Oh, this?

15:33.780 --> 15:36.260
<i>Whoo! Nice to meet you!</i>

15:36.260 --> 15:38.960
<i>We're Yuki and Aiko's mom and dad!</i>

15:38.960 --> 15:42.370
<i>We're in the middle of an excavation
at the Katsuyama ruins!</i>

15:42.370 --> 15:45.640
<i>Thanks for taking care of my family, everyone!</i>

15:45.640 --> 15:49.920
I've been introducing all of you
to my parents who work far away.

15:50.180 --> 15:52.290
Your parents seem kind.

15:52.290 --> 15:54.830
You said that's called a smartphone?

15:54.830 --> 15:55.890
It's amazing.

15:56.260 --> 15:58.860
It's like they're right here,
even when they're far away.

15:58.860 --> 16:01.730
Yeah, technology's awesome.

16:01.730 --> 16:05.160
Even with our bodies so far away,
our hearts are connected.

16:05.160 --> 16:07.520
Almost like you guys.

16:08.250 --> 16:13.030
You all came together here because
your hearts are connected!

16:13.990 --> 16:15.320
I think you're right!

16:15.320 --> 16:17.030
I'm so glad we made it here.

16:17.030 --> 16:18.540
This is all so fantastic!

16:18.540 --> 16:20.030
I'm happy, too!

16:22.920 --> 16:26.170
Yo, show me to my bed.

16:41.810 --> 16:43.200
Do you need something?

16:43.200 --> 16:44.070
Shit!

16:48.870 --> 16:51.600
Who're you calling the Otaku Club?

17:00.710 --> 17:02.130
Isn't this...

17:03.810 --> 17:04.770
Yes?

17:04.770 --> 17:05.970
Here we are.

17:06.990 --> 17:09.660
Assistant Principal... and...

17:13.000 --> 17:15.370
I think this is Mizuha's.

17:15.730 --> 17:19.960
I heard she was absent today,
but I believe she's at school.

17:22.870 --> 17:24.180
Guys, hear me out!

17:24.180 --> 17:26.490
The warriors of light are at my place!

17:25.620 --> 17:28.510
Aoki-kun, Mizuha's gone missing.

17:28.510 --> 17:29.980
As of two days ago.

17:31.860 --> 17:33.720
I'll go find her.

17:34.370 --> 17:35.480
Me, too.

17:45.040 --> 17:48.310
I thought her leg was still hurt.

17:50.360 --> 17:52.900
Sorry, Mizuha-chan.

17:52.900 --> 17:54.070
Are you okay?

17:54.070 --> 17:55.540
You sprained your ankle, didn't you?

17:55.880 --> 17:57.520
Don't sweat it.

18:01.260 --> 18:03.680
Why are <i>you</i> crying, Saki?!

18:03.680 --> 18:04.720
Because...

18:04.720 --> 18:08.860
I've liked him from way before!

18:06.070 --> 18:08.150
Cut it out. Come on!

18:09.690 --> 18:10.820
Fuuna!

18:12.930 --> 18:14.950
I'll get the teacher.

18:19.040 --> 18:20.120
Mizuha.

18:20.120 --> 18:22.320
Hanna. What's the matter?

18:22.620 --> 18:26.250
Nothing. I just saw you when
you fell, and I got worried.

18:30.170 --> 18:32.130
H-Hey...

18:32.130 --> 18:35.580
If there's anything on your mind or
if there's something bothering you,

18:35.580 --> 18:38.350
let me know, and I'll do whatever I can.

18:38.350 --> 18:39.750
You can always count on me.

18:40.330 --> 18:43.710
I consider you my friend, Mizuha.

18:57.650 --> 19:02.610
Then will you cry for me if I die?

19:11.010 --> 19:12.070
Yeah.

19:13.460 --> 19:14.870
Of course I would.

19:14.870 --> 19:17.020
Sorry for creeping you out.

19:18.380 --> 19:20.220
Thanks for coming to see me.

19:20.220 --> 19:22.130
I'm going to take the rest of the day off.

19:26.890 --> 19:28.340
So heavy!

19:28.340 --> 19:30.100
Weak.

19:31.580 --> 19:32.960
Are you all right?

19:33.510 --> 19:35.200
W-Want me to help?

19:35.200 --> 19:38.140
Who's making you carry all that?

19:40.310 --> 19:45.110
Er, I just transferred to
this school today, and...

19:51.750 --> 19:53.340
Looks like it's going to rain.

19:53.650 --> 19:55.960
I hope Onii-chan's okay.

19:55.960 --> 19:57.780
He's on grocery duty today.

20:03.840 --> 20:06.290
You're so good at that. Wow.

20:06.580 --> 20:08.190
Thanks.

20:08.190 --> 20:10.400
You can have this if you want.

20:10.400 --> 20:12.510
I want that one.

20:13.390 --> 20:15.510
It's my birthday today.

20:15.510 --> 20:16.940
Okay.

20:16.940 --> 20:19.020
It's your birthday gift, then.

20:21.930 --> 20:24.110
She's not here, either.

20:26.670 --> 20:30.490
I'm sorry, there's someone else I like.

20:31.670 --> 20:34.640
Your eighth confession this year?

20:34.640 --> 20:36.640
Who's this person you say you like?

20:36.640 --> 20:39.590
You've been rejecting everyone
for their sake, right?

20:39.590 --> 20:42.550
What? No way, I'm not saying.

20:42.550 --> 20:43.800
Give me a hint.

20:43.800 --> 20:45.190
I'm not telling.

20:45.190 --> 20:47.920
Hanna-chan, got a minute?

20:48.470 --> 20:50.320
Okay, I'll see you later.

20:50.320 --> 20:52.230
Okay.

20:52.820 --> 20:55.650
Hanna-chan, are you close friends with her?

20:55.650 --> 20:58.940
Well... normal friends, I guess.

20:59.200 --> 21:01.960
Everyone says you should stay away from her.

21:01.960 --> 21:02.890
Didn't you know?

21:03.570 --> 21:05.500
So you didn't know.

21:05.500 --> 21:10.530
That girl took A-chan's boyfriend,
and then she started flirting with Saji-kun.

21:10.530 --> 21:12.000
Can you believe her?

21:12.000 --> 21:13.070
Right?

21:13.070 --> 21:16.470
Apparently she was walking by the station
with a guy from Class 3 the other day.

21:16.470 --> 21:17.660
For real?

21:17.660 --> 21:20.800
Uno-senpai and Umocchan said the same thing.

21:20.800 --> 21:22.450
She stole their boyfriends.

21:22.450 --> 21:23.510
Yup, yup.

21:23.510 --> 21:27.310
So you should be careful, too, Hanna-chan.

21:27.990 --> 21:29.360
You're all idiots.

21:29.360 --> 21:31.760
She doesn't have time for that.

21:31.760 --> 21:32.760
Scary.

21:33.080 --> 21:34.510
What a loser.

21:43.140 --> 21:44.110
Here's a hint.

21:45.640 --> 21:47.240
Someone in my club.

21:56.010 --> 21:59.690
<i>Will you cry for me if I die?</i>

22:04.290 --> 22:08.680
<i>I couldn't respond right away when she asked.</i>

22:10.920 --> 22:12.010
I'm sorry.

22:13.620 --> 22:17.010
Mizuha! Mizuha!

22:17.980 --> 22:19.640
Mizuha!

22:20.320 --> 22:21.940
Mizuha!

22:22.670 --> 22:24.980
Mizuha!

22:24.980 --> 22:27.010
Please say something if you're there!

22:27.010 --> 22:28.810
Mizuha!

22:29.980 --> 22:32.450
<i>Where are you, Mizuha?</i>

22:33.030 --> 22:34.360
<i>Where are you?</i>

22:39.040 --> 22:41.050
Ow...

22:45.350 --> 22:47.020
My glasses...

22:47.020 --> 22:48.010
Are you okay?

22:48.320 --> 22:50.150
Looks like you aren't hurt.

22:50.150 --> 22:51.160
That's a relief.

22:53.000 --> 22:54.140
Thanks.

24:29.990 --> 24:55.010
<b>Preview</b>

24:31.860 --> 24:35.640
<i>Yuki and the others search for Mizuha.</i>

24:36.740 --> 24:42.370
<i>The lonely girl learns of the
legend of the immortal freak.</i>

24:44.020 --> 24:46.660
<i>A gift from mother to daughter</i>

24:47.370 --> 24:51.560
<i>becomes the thing that 
sets a tragedy in motion.</i>

24:52.010 --> 24:55.010
Mizuha
